resume: An extensive critique of Hegel’s attempt to unify philosophy from a European viewpoint, based on his Introduction to the Lectures on the History of Philosophy. The article argues for multiple origins of philosophy against Hegel’s single European vision, while acknowledging that some of his views remain relevant.
